l Palace](/wiki/National_Palace_(Mexico) \"National Palace (Mexico)\"). It is almost identical to his illustration done a decade and a half before. The war scene Nebel presents is closer to the reality on the ground, where the conquering U.S. forces were not welcomed by the resident population, particularly by a street person (*lépero*) about to hurl a rock at the invaders.[[6]](#cite_note-6) Although Kendall\\'s text and Nebel\\'s illustrations attempt to be true to the accounts of battle, there is no evidence that either one was at the [Battle of Buena Vista](/wiki/Battle_of_Buena_Vista \"Battle of Buena Vista\"), located in a remote part of northern Mexico.[[7]](#cite_note-7) Kendall was a correspondent and saw the [Battle of Molino del Rey](/wiki/Battle_of_Molino_del_Rey \"Battle of Molino del Rey\"), but Nebel was not. The battle is often not depicted in contemporary illustrations, but Nebel did two different views of it.[[8]](#cite_note-8)\\n\\nGallery\\n-------\\n\\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Carl_Nebel&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Gallery\")]\\n\\n* [![Las Tortilleras, published 1836](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Tortilleras_Nebel.jpg/120px-Tortilleras_Nebel.jpg)](/wiki/File:Tortilleras_Nebel.jpg \"Las Tortilleras, published 1836\")\\n  *Las Tortilleras*, published 1836\\n* [![Sierra Indians, published 1836](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Nebel_Voyage_41_Indias_de_la_Sierra.jpg/120px-Nebel_Voyage_41_Indias_de_la_Sierra.jpg)](/wiki/File:Nebel_Voyage_41_Indias_de_la_Sierra.jpg \"Sierra Indians, published 1836\")\\n  Sierra ', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 3, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Carl Nebel (1805-1855) was a German painter, engineer, architect, and draughtsman renowned for his detailed depictions of Mexican landscapes and people, especially during the Mexican–American War. After studying in Hamburg and Paris, Nebel moved to Mexico in 1829, where 